WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.958
Book Two, Proposition Six.

2
00:00:01.958 --> 00:00:18.282
If a segment be bisected, and a segment be added to it in a straight line, the rectangle contained by the whole with the added segment and the added segment, together with the square on the half, is equal to the square on the segment made up of the half and the added segment.

3
00:00:18.282 --> 00:00:23.250
Let the segment A B be bisected at C, and let B D be added to it in a straight line.

4
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:30.073
On C D, describe the square C E F D by One Forty-Six, and join the diagonal D E.

5
00:00:30.073 --> 00:00:42.320
Through B, draw B G parallel to E C or D F by One Thirty-One; through H, draw K M parallel to A B or E F; and through A, draw A K parallel to C L or D M.

6
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:48.592
Because A C equals C B, the rectangle A L equals C H by One Thirty-Six.

7
00:00:48.592 --> 00:00:57.988
By One Forty-Three, the complements about the diagonal are equal, so C H equals H F, and therefore A L equals H F.

8
00:00:57.988 --> 00:01:03.593
Adding C M to each, the whole rectangle A M equals the gnomon N O P.

9
00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:13.567
Since D M equals D B, A M is the rectangle contained by A D and D B; thus the gnomon N O P equals the rectangle A D, D B.

10
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:17.605
Add L G, which equals the square on C B, to each.

11
00:01:17.605 --> 00:01:23.540
Together, the gnomon N O P and L G form the whole square C E F D on C D.

12
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:32.524
Therefore, the rectangle contained by A D and D B, together with the square on C B, equals the square on C D.

13
00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:34.420
Which was to be proved.

14
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:40.929
Proposition Two Six is the geometric engine for solving quadratic equations by completing the square.

15
00:01:40.929 --> 00:01:57.388
Calling the half-segment a and the extension b, the rectangle two a plus b by b, plus a squared, equals the square on a plus b—allowing Greek geometers from Hippocrates of Chios onward to apply a rectangle exceeding by a square to solve a x plus x squared equals b squared.

16
00:01:57.388 --> 00:02:08.120
In the GEOMETOR G-Index, node G eighty-eight synthesizes nine direct prerequisites across fifty-four ancestor nodes, uniting Book One's complement theorem with Book Two's gnomon.

17
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:20.609
